<title>USA: FSA qualifies eight municipal issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies eight municipal issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said it has qualified for bond insurance the following nine municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Verona Township BOE, N.J., $7.5 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Oneonta City School District, N.Y., $6.663 million bonds.</p>
<p>--Wyandanch, N.Y., USFD, $11.08 million school district GOs.</p>
<p>--McKinney, Texas, $1.91 million revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--McKinney, Texas, $1.75 million wastewater and sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--Grosse Pointe Woods, Mich., $3.950 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Seattle, Wash., $55 million water revs.</p>
<p>--Tullahoma, Tenn., $7.125 million GOs.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
